From d44a80cefd03d50d9cd28408cc6b26cffa97d8ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 15:31:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/53] kaiair: sigma compensation (FPE-normalized DL stats),
 UL LDP delivery counters, UL cushion floor

- DL sigma estimator now measures the CHANNEL, not the controller: reports are
  normalized to full-power-equivalent SINR using the offset in force during the
  measured slot (1-report delay alignment; ambiguous-window updates skipped);
  loop input = FPE EWMA mean - live offset; GUI target mirrored from the loop
- UL LDP delivery classification at the CRC final outcome (ue_event_manager,
  SRB exempt), symmetric to DL; JSON renamed/split ldp_dl_* + ldp_ul_*;
  dl_pwr_shed_db emitted (DL actuator telemetry)
- KAIAIR_PKTR_MIN_CUSHION_DB (default 3): floor on the UL Cantelli cushion.
  Bench-measured: LDP D=20 collapses k(beta) to 0.88 -> ~1 dB margin -> CRC/
  sigma churn and link drops (9 in 10 min); with the floor the loop pins SINR
  on gamma+3 cleanly. A/B/C arms showed remaining drops are power-level
  self-interference (UE TX noise raises its own DL floor >10 dB p90), not LDP:
  LDP-on power-off = 0 drops in 10 min
